WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.460
A patient sits at a table, with
a screen hiding both hands.

2
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.010
A key is placed in their right hand.

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.900
Straight away, they say: a key.

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.810
Now the same key goes into the left hand.

5
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.040
Silence.

6
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.470
They can't name it.

7
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.380
Yet that left hand can pick the
key out from a tray of objects.

8
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.430
So why can they name it in one hand only?

9
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.550
In this mission, you'll see
how each hemisphere controls,

10
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.160
and feels touch from, the
opposite side of the body.

11
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.000
You'll meet the corpus callosum, the band
of nerve fibres joining the two hemispheres,

12
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.680
and why surgeons sometimes cut it.

13
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: explain why a split-brain
patient names the key in one hand only.
